   ],
   "rdfs:label": "Mehrabian's 7-38-55 rule",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "7%-38%-55% rule",
    "7-38-55 rule",
    "93% nonverbal myth",
    "Mehrabian myth",
    "communication is 93% nonverbal"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "cm:nonverbal-communication"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The popular claim that only 7% of a message's meaning comes from words, 38% from tone of voice and 55% from facial expression and body language; it overgeneralises two narrow 1967 lab studies about inconsistent cues for liking, and Mehrabian himself says it does not apply to communication in general.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/nonverbal-and-voice"
   },
